<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>When to Choose the Strawberry Sundae</h2>
    <p>The Strawberry Sundae is the best pick when you want a fruit-forward dessert that feels lighter than chocolate or caramel. The fresh strawberry topping is sweet, slightly tart, and cooling — a natural fit after a heavier meal like a <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger">FlameThrower Stackburger</a> or a <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">Chicken Strip Basket</a>. The 280 calories make it one of the more balanced dessert choices on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Sundae vs. Blizzard — What's the Right Dessert?</h2>
    <p>If you want a simple, lighter dessert, the Strawberry Sundae at $3.79 wins. If you want something more substantial and complex, a <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Mini Oreo Blizzard</a> at $3.49 is actually slightly cheaper while delivering the full Blizzard experience. The Sundae is better as a complement to a full meal. The Blizzard is better as a standalone dessert.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Dessert</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Strawberry Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>280</td><td>Light after-meal treat, fruity</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Hot Fudge Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>300</td><td>Classic warm-cold chocolate contrast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Caramel Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>310</td><td>Rich, sweet caramel lovers</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Oreo Blizzard (Mini)</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>~300</td><td>Full Blizzard experience, lower price</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$2.39</td><td>230</td><td>Lightest and cheapest option</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Strawberry Sundae in the $7 Meal Deal</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> includes a Small Sundae as its dessert component — and you can choose Strawberry. At 280 cal, it is the lowest-calorie sundae option in the deal, making it a smart pick if you want to keep the total meal calorie count in check. The full $7 Meal Deal gives you a cheeseburger or 3-piece chicken strips, fries, a drink, and this sundae for $7.00.</p>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ask for extra topping:</strong> Some locations will add a second pour of strawberry topping at a small upcharge. If you love the strawberry flavor, it is worth asking.</li>
      <li><strong>Temperature matters:</strong> Eat the sundae quickly. Soft serve warms faster than hard ice cream, and the strawberry topping accelerates the melt. Order it last in your meal sequence.</li>
      <li><strong>Pair with a lighter entrée:</strong> The Strawberry Sundae works best as a complement to a <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">cheeseburger</a> or <a href="/items/chili-cheese-dog">Chili Dog</a> — not after a full Chicken Strip Basket where the calorie total would be very high.</li>
    </ul>

